# Specify files that shouldn't be modified by Fern
README.md
.github/assets/logo.png

# Hand-written flows CreateAndWait helpers (client.Flows.Image.CreateAndWait, and on .Video,
# .TextToSpeech and .Templates.Runs): start a generation or template run, then poll Get until it is
# completed or failed, honouring Retry-After. The generator does not emit them. Each method lives in
# its own file in the generated package, so no generated file is edited; the shared polling loop is
# in flows/internal/flowswait. Matches the Python, TypeScript, Rust and .NET SDKs.
flows/create_and_wait.go
flows/create_and_wait_test.go
flows/image/create_and_wait.go
flows/video/create_and_wait.go
flows/texttospeech/create_and_wait.go
flows/templates/runs/create_and_wait.go
flows/internal/flowswait/

# Hand-written webhook signature verifier. Fern's built-in verifier can't parse the compound
# `ElevenLabs-Signature: t=...,v0=...` header, so this matches the Python/Rust/.NET SDKs by hand.
# It adds the package-level `webhooks.ConstructEvent` and a `ConstructEvent` method on the
# generated `webhooks.Client` (Go lets a package's methods live in any of its files), so no
# generated file is edited.
webhooks/verifier.go
webhooks/verifier_test.go
